# Cursor & AI IDE Rules — Echo Link-Tree

All AI coding assistants (Cursor, ChatGPT, Windsurf, Claude, Copilot, Antigravity) must strictly follow these rules:

> **SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH**: [`link-tree/AGENTS.md`](file:///Users/Shared/projeckt/goto/link-tree/AGENTS.md) is the authoritative rulebook. Always read `link-tree/AGENTS.md` before making architectural or code changes.

## 1. Coding Standards & Conventions
- **Strict Patterns**: Adhere strictly to established architectural patterns, folder structures, and conventions in the codebase.
- **Git Commits**: Conventional Commits specification (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `style:`, `docs:`, `test:`).
- **CSS / BEM**: Use strict BEM (`Block__Element--Modifier`) naming conventions for all CSS classes. Never use ID selectors for styling.
- **Minimal HTML**: Keep HTML semantic and minimal. Omit redundant wrapper elements, unused attributes, and boilerplate bloat.
- **Dependencies**: Vet external packages for high adoption and maintenance. Never install trivial one-liner micro-dependencies (`is-odd`, `left-pad`).

## 2. Core Architectural Invariants
- **Pure Static Output**: Pre-rendered HTML via Eleventy (11ty) v3.x and Dart Sass. Zero client-side framework hydration (no React, Vue, Svelte, Alpine).
- **Strict Privacy (DSGVO)**: Zero initial third-party connections. Self-hosted fonts (`Clash Display`, `Inter`). No cookies on initial visit. 2-click consent YouTube facade via `youtube-nocookie.com`.
- **Brand Color Constancy**: Colors (`#08415C` Dark Teal Blue, `#846B8A` Muted Lavender, `#FEFADC` Light Pastel Yellow) never change across routes.
- **Logo Clear Space**: Clear buffer equal to lowercase `"e"` on all four sides. Never distort or rotate.
- **External Legal Links**: Impressum and Datenschutz point to canonical external URLs (`https://kirche-echo.de/...`). Local routes must never be served.
- **Interactivity**: Pure CSS `<details>` / `<summary>` for collapsible cards (`DropdownCard`).
- **Accessibility (a11y) Suite**: Skip link, floating trigger, HTML5 dialog for font scaling & 21:1 high contrast modes, mobile fixed positioning, and scroll locking.

## 3. Verification Sequence
Always run before reporting task completion:
```bash
npm run validate
npm run build
npm test
```
All 55+ test assertions must pass with 0 errors.
